Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: skip ROM firmware setup for Green2 flash boot

The AmebaGreen2 0bda:f851 composite device runs its controller firmware
from the module's own flash. The generic Realtek vendor match calls
btrtl_setup_realtek(), which sends unsupported ROM-loader commands and
can reset the entire composite device, including the active WHC NIC.

Match this device before the Realtek wildcard and retain generic HCI USB
handling. This is for the flash-boot NAN + BT INIC USB configuration;
it is not a replacement firmware loader for ROM-download configurations.

Validated against Ubuntu linux-source-7.0.0 7.0.0-38.38.
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -611,6 +611,12 @@ static const struct usb_device_id quirks_table[] = {
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x0489, 0xe130), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
 						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
 
+	/* AmebaGreen2 flash-boot composite: controller firmware is already
+	 * loaded by the module. Do not run Realtek ROM firmware download.
+	 * Keep this entry before the vendor-wide Realtek match below.
+	 */
+	{ USB_DEVICE_INTERFACE_CLASS(0x0bda, 0xf851, 0xe0) },
+
 	/* Realtek Bluetooth devices */
 	{ USB_VENDOR_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(0x0bda, 0xe0, 0x01, 0x01),
 	  .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK },
